From 5f48dba44b955acba5da4ed78f9587a1d437441a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:30:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(ledger): macOS may undo its own tile when the displays
 change; Notes and Mail stop at one of two sizes

Two facts about Macs, read out of hosted Macs' recordings.

- At some changes of displays macOS gives a window it had tiled the frame
  from the moment before the tile. After a drag to an edge that frame hangs
  over the edge. Seven windows in one journey, with Arbor and without.
- Asked for less, Notes stops at 300 or at 320 high and Mail at 881 or at
  871 wide, and the two go together: five runs of five. The stand-ins'
  table keeps 320 with 871, a pair that was seen together.
---
