+### macos-may-undo-its-own-tile-when-the-displays-change
+
+*hurt 2 · at the seam · touches `size-lost`*
+
+- **Expected:** A window that macOS has tiled stays as it is when a display is plugged in or unplugged, or comes to the display that is left in the size it had.
+- **Happened:** At some changes of displays macOS gives a window it had tiled the frame from the moment before the tile, place and size, to the point (once a point off) and mostly in one step. After a drag to an edge that frame hangs over the edge, where the hand held the window. In one journey, played three times: Calendar, let go at the right edge at 1284,300 937×600 and tiled to 800,32 801×791, was back at 1284,300 937×600 at the next plug, standing on the main display, with a third of its width in view; without Arbor the same at 1266,355 and at 1277,438. Mail without Arbor: 1069,270 1120×630 before the tile, back there when the display went that macOS had taken it to; in the other playing 1040,270, at an unplug, on the main display. Terminal without Arbor: 1165,398 863×499. Preview with Arbor: docked at 12,433 1576×377, dragged at that size to the left edge, last at -768,438, tiled to -1,31 804×791, sent across by Arbor at 2159,160 802×791; when that display went it was back at -768,438 1576×377, 49 % of it off the left edge and in the size of an Arbor slot, and it stayed so through `home` and Quit. Arbor set it no frame. Not at every change: Preview kept its tile through an unplug and a plug before that, and through three changes in each playing without Arbor. What decides is not known. With a docked window dragged to an edge it is `macos-remembers-a-tile-arbor-has-undone` set off by something else, and the place comes back as well.
+- **Found by:** A journey with a second, virtual display played without Arbor, with it and without it again on one hosted Mac, macOS 26.6.2, on 2026-10-15: seven windows' roads read out of the three playings' samples, and Arbor's trace, in which no request asks for any of those frames. Counted by three readers apart.
+- **Stand-ins play it:** **no** (`FakeWindowSystem.takeSizeBeforeTile`)
+- **Guard:** **none**
+- **Arbor copes:** **not yet**
+- **Read in:** `scripts/mac-shell/lib-walk.sh`, `scripts/mac-shell/jolts.py`
+
