+### notes-and-mail-stop-at-one-of-two-sizes-and-go-together
+
+*hurt 4 · at the seam*
+
+- **Expected:** An app has one smallest size, so that one measurement is enough for a table or a store.
+- **Happened:** Asked for less, Notes stopped at 300 high in some runs and at 320 in others, and Mail at 881 wide or at 871. In the five runs that asked both they went together: 320 with 871 twice, 300 with 881 three times. In one of those three the same window of Notes answered 300 and, 23 seconds later, asked for exactly 709×300, answered 709×320, twice. A survey that asked every app once got 709×300 from Notes and no answer from Mail. What sets the state is not known. A rehearsal with the table at 320 differed from a Mac that answered 300 in one slot of nine after `arrange`, by 20 points, at six acts of fifty.
+- **Found by:** Every request for a frame and its answer in 161 recordings of hosted Macs, macOS 26.6.2, between 23:21 UTC on 2026-10-14 and 14:34 UTC on 2026-10-15; counted twice, by two readers apart.
+- **Stand-ins play it:** partly (`RealApp.minimum`)
+- **Guard:** **none**
+- **Arbor copes:** Sources/ArborTesting/RealApps.swift has 709×320 and 871×236, a pair that was seen together. Arbor itself asks and goes by the answer; a size that is kept from one day for another can be 20 or 10 points off.
+- **Read in:** `Sources/ArborTesting/RealApps.swift`, `scripts/mac-shell/walk-diff.py`
